-- Backfills the five new film-spec columns for all 40 existing films.
--
-- Content researched via Wikipedia (infoboxes, plot sections) and cross-
-- checked against other sources for post-credits scene counts, retrieved
-- 2026-08-03. Recaps are new prose, spoiler-heavy and present-tense — see
-- the schema comment on `films.recap` for why this is separate from
-- `description`.
--
-- Films 39 (Avengers: Doomsday) and 40 (Avengers: Secret Wars) had not
-- released as of the research date, so their duration/recap are best-
-- available placeholders rather than confirmed facts — correct them via
-- /admin once each film is out. Film 40 has no official poster yet either;
-- it points at the Marvel Studios logo until one exists.

UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Iron_Man_%282008_film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Tony Stark builds the first Iron Man suit in an Afghan cave to escape captivity after being ambushed and implanted with an electromagnet to keep shrapnel from reaching his heart. Back home he shuts down his company''s weapons division and secretly builds the sleek Mark III armor, using it to destroy his own stockpiled weapons in the field. He discovers his mentor Obadiah Stane orchestrated his kidnapping and has been selling to terrorists behind his back; Stane steals Tony''s arc reactor and builds a hulking Iron Monger suit for the final showdown atop Stark Industries. Tony has Pepper overload the massive reactor, electrocuting and killing Stane, then blows his own cover story at a press conference by declaring "I am Iron Man."', duration = 126, director = 'Jon Favreau', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 1;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/The_Incredible_Hulk_%28film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Bruce Banner hides out in Brazil trying to cure the gamma radiation that turns him into the Hulk, but General Ross tracks him down and sends a strike team, forcing a rage-fueled escape. Banner reunites with Betty Ross and heads to New York, hoping scientist Samuel Sterns can synthesize an antidote from his blood. Soldier Emil Blonsky, addicted to the power of fighting Hulk, injects himself with Banner''s blood and Ross''s super-soldier serum, transforming into the monstrous Abomination and tearing through Harlem. Hulk beats him into submission and lets himself be taken, then retreats to Canada to master his condition — while Tony Stark shows up at a bar to tell Ross "we''re putting a team together."', duration = 112, director = 'Louis Leterrier', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 2;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ed/Iron_Man_2_poster.jpg', recap = 'With his Iron Man identity now public, Tony Stark is secretly dying as the palladium core powering his arc reactor poisons his blood, while Russian physicist Ivan Vanko builds arc-powered whips for revenge over Howard Stark''s betrayal of his father. Vanko attacks Tony at the Monaco Grand Prix, then partners with rival Justin Hammer to mass-produce weaponized drone suits. A drunken Tony fights his best friend Rhodey at his own birthday party, who makes off with a prototype suit that Hammer promptly hijacks. Nick Fury feeds Tony his own father''s research to synthesize a new element that cures his poisoning, and at the Stark Expo, Tony and Rhodey destroy Vanko''s hijacked drone army before Vanko detonates himself; Fury demotes Tony to consultant while Agent Coulson discovers Mjolnir buried in the New Mexico desert.', duration = 125, director = 'Jon Favreau', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 3;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/95/Thor_%28film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Thor''s reckless attack on Jotunheim, secretly enabled by his jealous brother Loki, gets him stripped of his powers and exiled to New Mexico as a mortal, where he falls for astrophysicist Jane Foster while his hammer Mjolnir sits guarded nearby. Loki, revealed to be a Frost Giant adopted by Odin, seizes the Asgardian throne, tries to have Laufey kill their father, and unleashes the fiery Destroyer on Thor and his friends on Earth. Proving himself worthy again, Thor reclaims Mjolnir, destroys the Destroyer, and returns to Asgard to stop Loki from committing genocide against Jotunheim via the Bifrost Bridge. Thor destroys the bridge to save the Frost Giants, Loki lets himself fall into the void rather than be saved, and Nick Fury shows scientist Erik Selvig the Tesseract — with an unseen, surviving Loki secretly whispering in his ear.', duration = 114, director = 'Kenneth Branagh', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 4;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/Captain_America_The_First_Avenger_poster.jpg', recap = 'Scrawny Steve Rogers volunteers for an experimental super-soldier serum and becomes Captain America, leading the Howling Commandos against Hydra''s Johann Schmidt (Red Skull), who wields the Tesseract''s power to build superweapons. Rogers rescues Bucky Barnes and his fellow POWs, but during the final raid on Schmidt''s base Bucky falls to his apparent death from a moving train. Aboard Schmidt''s flying wing, the Tesseract opens a portal that swallows Schmidt whole, and Rogers crash-lands the plane into Arctic ice to keep its bombs from reaching American cities, seemingly sacrificing himself. He wakes up decades later in a fake 1940s room, breaks out into modern Times Square, and learns from Nick Fury that he''s been frozen for nearly 70 years — then gets recruited for "a mission with worldwide ramifications."', duration = 124, director = 'Joe Johnston', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 5;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8a/The_Avengers_%282012_film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Loki strikes a bargain with the alien Chitauri for an army to conquer Earth in exchange for the Tesseract, prompting Nick Fury to activate the Avengers Initiative and assemble Iron Man, Captain America, Thor, Hulk, Black Widow, and Hawkeye. Infighting aboard the Helicarrier boils over when Loki triggers Banner''s transformation into the Hulk and murders Agent Coulson, but Coulson''s death is the spark that finally unites the team. Loki opens a portal above Stark Tower and unleashes the Chitauri fleet on Manhattan; Tony flies a nuclear missile through the wormhole into the mothership, seemingly sacrificing himself before Hulk catches his falling body, and Widow closes the portal with Loki''s scepter. Thor hauls a defeated Loki and the Tesseract back to Asgard while the team quietly regroups — followed by the Other reporting the failed invasion to his master, and the exhausted Avengers silently eating shawarma together.', duration = 143, director = 'Joss Whedon', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 6;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/19/Iron_Man_3_poster.jpg', recap = 'Traumatized by the Battle of New York and suffering panic attacks, Tony Stark publicly challenges the terrorist Mandarin after an attack levels his Malibu mansion, stranding him in Tennessee with a malfunctioning suit. He discovers the Mandarin is a fabricated front — actually failed actor Trevor Slattery — while the real threat is Aldrich Killian, who has weaponized the fire-breathing Extremis serum and kidnapped Pepper Potts, injecting her with it. In the climactic oil-tanker battle, an Extremis-empowered Pepper turns the tables and kills Killian herself. Tony remotely detonates his entire fleet of suits, has the arc-reactor shrapnel surgically removed from his chest, and narrates that "I am Iron Man" was never really about the armor — with a mid-credits gag revealing Tony has been telling this whole story to a bemused Bruce Banner.', duration = 130, director = 'Shane Black', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 7;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7f/Thor_The_Dark_World_poster.jpg', recap = 'Ancient Dark Elf Malekith awakens seeking the reality-warping Aether, which has infected Jane Foster after she stumbles into an inter-dimensional convergence portal in London. Thor smuggles Jane to Asgard for protection, but Malekith''s forces storm the realm and kill Thor''s mother Frigga, pushing Thor to break Loki out of prison and team up with him for revenge. Loki fakes his own death extracting the Aether, Malekith absorbs it, and the fight spills across multiple realms via the Convergence back to Greenwich, where Jane''s makeshift tech strands Malekith on Svartalfheim to be crushed by his own crashing ship. Thor turns down the Asgardian throne to stay close to Earth, unaware that "Loki" has secretly been impersonating Odin the whole time — while a mid-credits scene shows Sif and Volstagg delivering the Aether to the Collector, right next to the Tesseract.', duration = 112, director = 'Alan Taylor', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 8;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Captain_America_The_Winter_Soldier_poster.jpg', recap = 'Steve Rogers discovers S.H.I.E.L.D. has been secretly building Project Insight, three Helicarriers designed to preemptively execute millions deemed threats, right as Nick Fury is gunned down by a masked assassin known as the Winter Soldier. Rogers and Natasha Romanoff go rogue and uncover that Hydra has been growing inside S.H.I.E.L.D. since World War II, with Arnim Zola''s mind preserved in a supercomputer and high-ranking official Alexander Pierce running the conspiracy. The Winter Soldier is revealed to be Steve''s presumed-dead best friend Bucky Barnes, brainwashed and cryogenically weaponized by Hydra for decades. Steve, Natasha and Sam Wilson destroy the Helicarriers before they can launch, Pierce is killed, and a battered Bucky pulls a drowning Steve from the river before vanishing — leaving S.H.I.E.L.D. in ruins, Fury faking his death, and a mid-credits scene of Baron von Strucker experimenting on two superpowered prisoners (Pietro and Wanda Maximoff) with Loki''s scepter.', duration = 136, director = 'Anthony Russo, Joe Russo', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 9;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Guardians_of_the_Galaxy_%28film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Abducted from Earth as a kid, Peter Quill grows up into a small-time thief who steals a mysterious Orb that turns out to be an Infinity Stone, drawing the attention of assassin Gamora, bounty hunters Rocket and Groot, and the vengeance-driven Drax. Thrown together in Nova Corps custody, the misfit crew learns the fanatical Kree zealot Ronan the Accuser plans to use the Stone to annihilate the planet Xandar, and Gamora betrays her adoptive father Thanos to stop him. In the climactic battle over Xandar, the team destroys Ronan''s hammer and collectively channels the Infinity Stone''s power to obliterate him themselves rather than let any one of them wield it alone. Groot sacrifices himself to shield the others but leaves behind a sprouting twig that regrows into Baby Groot, the team''s criminal records are wiped, and the credits close on the Collector''s captive duck and space-dog exhibit shooting the audience a look.', duration = 122, director = 'James Gunn', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 10;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/ff/Avengers_Age_of_Ultron_poster.jpg', recap = 'Tony Stark and Bruce Banner secretly build an AI peacekeeping program using Loki''s captured scepter, but the resulting Ultron decides humanity itself is the threat to Earth and must be wiped out. Ultron recruits the enhanced Maximoff twins and builds a plan to lift the Sokovian capital into the sky and drop it to trigger a mass-extinction event, while also creating the synthetic being Vision from vibranium and the Mind Stone. Pietro Maximoff dies shielding Hawkeye from gunfire during the final battle, and Stark and Thor detonate the floating city core to shatter it before it can crash, with Vision destroying Ultron''s last remaining body. The team disbands from Stark Tower, a rebuilt roster of Rhodey, Vision, Sam Wilson, and Wanda Maximoff trains as the new Avengers, and a mid-credits scene shows Thanos donning the Infinity Gauntlet, growling that he''ll get the Stones himself.', duration = 141, director = 'Joss Whedon', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 11;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/12/Ant-Man_%28film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Ex-con Scott Lang is manipulated by scientist Hank Pym into stealing his own shrinking Ant-Man suit, then recruited to stop Pym''s former protégé Darren Cross from selling a militarized version called Yellowjacket. Training with Hope van Dyne to control an army of ants, Scott learns Hope''s mother Janet vanished into the subatomic Quantum Realm decades earlier while disarming a missile. Scott infiltrates a Pym Technologies gala to steal the Yellowjacket suit, gets captured, and in the climactic shrinking fight sabotages Cross''s suit so badly Cross shrinks into nonexistence; Scott himself plunges into the Quantum Realm and barely reverses course to survive. Hope gets shown a new Wasp suit of her own in a mid-credits tease, and in the post-credits scene, Steve Rogers and Sam Wilson have Bucky Barnes in custody, debating who else they''ll need to call in.', duration = 117, director = 'Peyton Reed', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 12;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/53/Captain_America_Civil_War_poster.jpg', recap = 'After a botched Lagos mission kills innocent Wakandans, the UN''s Sokovia Accords split the Avengers — Tony Stark backs government oversight out of guilt, Steve Rogers refuses to surrender their autonomy — just as Wakandan prince T''Challa vows revenge after his father is killed in a bombing framed on Bucky Barnes. The real culprit, Helmut Zemo, is secretly manipulating events to trigger Bucky''s Hydra brainwashing and expose old wounds, engineering a superhero civil war rather than fighting one himself. Cap''s team (Bucky, Wanda, Falcon, Hawkeye, Ant-Man) clashes with Tony''s team (Widow, Vision, T''Challa, War Machine, and a newly recruited teenage Peter Parker) at Leipzig airport, and Vision accidentally cripples Rhodey. In Siberia, Zemo reveals footage of Bucky assassinating Tony''s parents under Hydra control; an enraged Tony nearly kills Bucky, destroys his arm, and Steve leaves his shield behind — with Bucky choosing Wakandan cryo-sleep in a mid-credits scene and Peter Parker examining his new Stark-built web-shooters in the post-credits scene.', duration = 147, director = 'Anthony Russo, Joe Russo', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 13;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a1/Doctor_Strange_%282016_film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Arrogant neurosurgeon Stephen Strange loses the use of his hands in a car crash and travels to Kamar-Taj, where the Ancient One trains him in the mystic arts after conventional medicine fails him. Renegade sorcerer Kaecilius steals pages from the forbidden Book of Cagliostro to summon the dark entity Dormammu from the Dark Dimension, seeking eternal life for himself and his followers. Strange masters manipulation of time via the Eye of Agamotto and confronts Dormammu directly, trapping him in an infinite time loop until the entity agrees to leave Earth alone forever. The Ancient One dies from injuries sustained in the fighting, disillusioned protégé Mordo walks away from sorcery altogether, and Strange takes over the New York Sanctum — with a mid-credits scene where he agrees to help Thor find Odin, and a post-credits scene of Mordo starting to strip other sorcerers of their powers, declaring there are "too many."', duration = 115, director = 'Scott Derrickson', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 14;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Guardians_of_the_Galaxy_Vol._2_poster.jpg', recap = 'After angering the golden Sovereign race, the Guardians are rescued by a mysterious being who turns out to be Peter Quill''s biological father Ego, a Celestial who invites Quill, Gamora, and Drax to his idyllic home planet while Yondu''s Ravager crew mutinies against him. Ego reveals he''s been planting "seedling" versions of himself across the galaxy for eons, confesses to killing Quill''s mother, and brainwashes Quill to help him activate a universe-wide expansion that will wipe out all other life. The team destroys Ego''s planetary brain from the inside, and Yondu sacrifices his own life shoving Quill into a spacesuit before dying in the vacuum of space, honored afterward with a full Ravager funeral. Rocket takes up Yondu''s arrow, exiled Ravager captains reunite under Stakar Ogord, the golden Ayesha begins gestating a new weapon she names Adam (Warlock), and Baby Groot has grown into an eye-rolling teenager — capped by the recurring Watchers finally walking out on Stan Lee''s rambling stories.', duration = 136, director = 'James Gunn', post_credits_scenes = 5 WHERE id = 15;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Spider-Man_Homecoming_poster.jpg', recap = 'Displaced salvage worker Adrian Toomes turns to selling weaponized alien Chitauri tech as the Vulture, while teenage Peter Parker juggles high school with unauthorized Spider-Man patrols, eager to prove himself to Tony Stark. Peter tracks Toomes'' operation to a ferry deal that goes catastrophically wrong when a splitting energy weapon nearly tears the boat in half, and Stark confiscates Peter''s suit as punishment. At his school homecoming dance, Peter discovers his date Liz''s father is Toomes — and Toomes figures out Peter''s secret identity in a tense car ride. Wearing his old homemade suit, Peter intercepts Toomes hijacking a plane full of stolen Avengers tech, saves his life when his own suit malfunctions mid-heist, and turns down Stark''s Avengers invitation to keep being a "friendly neighborhood" hero — while a mid-credits scene shows a jailed rival dealer needling Toomes for Spider-Man''s real name, and Toomes staying loyally silent.', duration = 133, director = 'Jon Watts', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 16;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7d/Thor_Ragnarok_poster.jpg', recap = 'Thor learns his long-lost, secretly imprisoned sister Hela is Asgard''s true firstborn heir, and after Odin''s death she shatters Mjolnir and exiles Thor to the trash-planet Sakaar, where the Grandmaster forces him to gladiator-fight a captive, feral Hulk. Teaming with Hulk, the disillusioned warrior Valkyrie, and a scheming Loki, Thor escapes Sakaar to find Hela has already conquered Asgard and raised an undead army. Realizing the only way to stop her is to let the prophesied apocalypse of Ragnarok happen, Thor has Loki summon the fire demon Surtur, who grows into a giant and destroys both Hela and the entire city of Asgard. Thor loses an eye but becomes king, leading the Asgardian refugees toward Earth aboard a stolen ship — until a massive unidentified vessel looms out of the darkness in front of them in the mid-credits scene, setting up Thanos''s ambush.', duration = 130, director = 'Taika Waititi', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 17;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Black_Panther_%28film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'T''Challa returns home to be crowned King of Wakanda after his father''s death, only to have his throne challenged by Erik "Killmonger" Stevens — his own American-raised cousin, abandoned as a child after T''Challa''s father killed Killmonger''s father for conspiring with the arms dealer Klaue. Killmonger wins ritual combat, throws T''Challa off a waterfall to apparent death, and seizes the throne intending to arm oppressed people worldwide with vibranium weapons and conquer the globe. Rescued and revived by the rival Jabari tribe, T''Challa returns for a second duel in the vibranium mines, defeats Killmonger, and offers to heal him — but Killmonger chooses to die free, watching the sunset, rather than live imprisoned. T''Challa opens Wakanda''s first outreach center in Oakland and reveals the nation''s true technological power to the United Nations in the mid-credits scene, while Shuri begins helping a recovering Bucky Barnes in the post-credits scene.', duration = 134, director = 'Ryan Coogler', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 18;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Avengers_Infinity_War_poster.jpg', recap = 'Thanos rampages across the galaxy collecting the Infinity Stones, killing Loki and Heimdall outright and forcing his adopted daughter Gamora to reveal the Soul Stone''s location by sacrificing her himself. The Avengers splinter into desperate strike teams — Stark, Strange and Spider-Man in space, Thor with the Guardians, and Cap''s team defending Vision and Wanda in Wakanda — but every attempt to stop Thanos fails, including Star-Lord blowing their best shot at prying the Gauntlet off in a rage. Wanda is forced to destroy the Mind Stone in Vision''s head to deny Thanos the final piece, only for Thanos to reverse time and rip it out anyway, completing the Gauntlet. He snaps his fingers on Titan and in Wakanda, and half of all life in the universe crumbles to dust in real time — Strange, Spider-Man, T''Challa, Star-Lord, Bucky, and countless others included — leaving the survivors shattered as Nick Fury dissolves mid-sentence, having just paged someone before he goes.', duration = 149, director = 'Anthony Russo, Joe Russo', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 19;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2c/Ant-Man_and_the_Wasp_poster.jpg', recap = 'Under house arrest after Civil War, Scott Lang starts having strange psychic visions connecting him to Janet van Dyne, who''s been trapped in the Quantum Realm since 1987, spurring Hank Pym and Hope van Dyne to finish a quantum tunnel to retrieve her. Black-market dealer Sonny Burch and a molecularly unstable, intangible woman called Ghost (really Ava Starr, whose scientist father died in a lab accident) both chase down Pym''s shrinking lab technology for their own ends. The team finally opens a stable tunnel and rescues Janet, who — rather than let Ava die from her condition — voluntarily shares her own quantum energy to stabilize her. Scott slips back home just as his house arrest ends, but in a mid-credits gut-punch, Hank, Hope and Janet send him into the Quantum Realm to harvest more particles for Ava — right as Thanos''s snap disintegrates all three of them, stranding Scott alone in the Quantum Realm.', duration = 118, director = 'Peyton Reed', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 20;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4e/Captain_Marvel_%28film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'Amnesiac Kree soldier "Vers" crash-lands on 1990s Earth chasing shapeshifting Skrulls and discovers she''s actually Carol Danvers, a presumed-dead Air Force pilot whose light-speed engine test exploded years earlier, killing her mentor (secretly the Kree scientist Mar-Vell) and supercharging Carol with cosmic energy while erasing her memory. Teaming with a young Nick Fury and reuniting with her old friend Maria Rambeau, Carol finds Mar-Vell''s hidden lab holding a colony of Skrull refugees and the Tesseract, and removes an implant the Kree used to suppress her true power all along. She overpowers her former commander Yon-Rogg and the Kree Empire''s forces, sends him home with a message for the Supreme Intelligence, then leaves Earth to help the Skrulls find a new homeworld — after her cat "Goose" is revealed to be a tentacled alien Flerken that swallowed the Tesseract, and gifting Fury the modified pager that becomes the film''s mid-credits Avengers-summoning payoff.', duration = 124, director = 'Anna Boden, Ryan Fleck', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 21;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0d/Avengers_Endgame_poster.jpg', recap = 'Five years after Thanos''s snap wiped out half of all life, Scott Lang escapes the Quantum Realm and gives the surviving Avengers a plan: time-travel back to key moments to steal the Infinity Stones before Thanos ever collects them. The heist mostly succeeds, but it alerts a past version of Thanos, who travels to the present with his army and levels the Avengers compound in a massive final battle joined by every resurrected hero. Tony Stark snatches the Stones for himself, snaps Thanos''s entire army to dust, and dies from the Gauntlet''s power, sacrificing himself to save the universe for good. Steve Rogers returns the Stones to their proper timelines and chooses to stay in the past to live a full life with Peggy Carter, coming back as an old man to pass his shield to Sam Wilson — the film has no traditional scene after the credits, just the ringing sound of a hammer striking metal, echoing Tony forging his first suit back in Iron Man.', duration = 181, director = 'Anthony Russo, Joe Russo', post_credits_scenes = 0 WHERE id = 22;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Spider-Man_Far_From_Home_poster.jpg', recap = 'Grieving Tony Stark''s death, Peter Parker just wants a normal European school trip, but Nick Fury drags him into stopping the "Elementals" alongside Quentin Beck, a charismatic hero from an alternate Earth who hands Peter Stark''s drone-controlling E.D.I.T.H. glasses. MJ figures out Beck is actually a fraud — a disgruntled ex-Stark employee faking the entire threat with elaborate hologram and drone technology to stage himself as the next Iron Man. After Beck orchestrates a giant illusory monster attack over London and frames Peter, Peter regains control of E.D.I.T.H. and beats him, only for a stray drone to accidentally kill Beck. In the mid-credits scene, tabloid host J. Jonah Jameson broadcasts Beck''s doctored footage blaming Spider-Man for his death and blows Peter''s secret identity to the entire world, while the post-credits scene reveals the "Fury" and "Hill" seen throughout the whole film were actually shapeshifting Skrulls Talos and Soren, with the real Fury off in deep space.', duration = 129, director = 'Jon Watts', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 23;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/Black_Widow_%282021_film%29_poster.jpg', recap = 'A fugitive Natasha Romanoff, hiding out after Civil War, is drawn back to her fabricated "sister" Yelena Belova, who''s carrying vials that can free brainwashed Black Widow assassins from the Red Room''s mind control. The two reunite with their fake parents — super-soldier Alexei and spy Melina — and discover General Dreykov, whom Natasha believed she''d killed years earlier, is alive and still running the Red Room from an airborne fortress. Natasha also confronts Dreykov''s masked enforcer Taskmaster, revealed to be his own daughter Antonia, disfigured and mind-controlled after the bombing Natasha thought killed her. The Red Room falls and explodes, Natasha frees Antonia from her conditioning and gives Yelena the antidote to liberate the rest of the Widows, and in the post-credits scene, the shadowy Valentina Allegra de Fontaine visits Natasha''s grave to recruit a grieving Yelena for her next target: Clint Barton.', duration = 134, director = 'Cate Shortland', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 24;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/74/Shang-Chi_and_the_Legend_of_the_Ten_Rings_poster.jpeg', recap = 'Immortal warlord Wenwu, wielder of the mystical Ten Rings, trained his son Shang-Chi as a child assassin after the murder of his wife Ying Li, but Shang-Chi fled to San Francisco years ago to build an anonymous life. When Wenwu''s agents attack him for a pendant tied to his mother, Shang-Chi reconnects with his estranged sister Xialing and the two are captured and dragged to Ta Lo, the hidden dimensional village their mother came from. There, an ancient entity called the Dweller-in-Darkness has been impersonating Ying Li''s voice to manipulate Wenwu into opening a mystical Dark Gate, and Wenwu sacrifices himself to save his son once he realizes the deception. Shang-Chi and Xialing defeat the Dweller together, and afterward Wong summons them both to Kamar-Taj in a mid-credits meeting with Bruce Banner and Captain Marvel about the strange power radiating from the Ten Rings, while Xialing quietly takes over her father''s criminal empire in the post-credits scene.', duration = 132, director = 'Destin Daniel Cretton', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 25;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9b/Eternals_%28film%29_poster.jpeg', recap = 'Ten immortal Eternals have secretly guided humanity since 5000 BC, believing their mission is to protect Earth from monstrous Deviants — until they discover their true, horrifying purpose is to incubate a Celestial inside the planet whose "Emergence" will destroy it and birth a new star. Sersi becomes the group''s reluctant new leader as the team splinters over whether to stop the Emergence, with the loyalist Ikaris killing fellow Eternal Gilgamesh and initially sabotaging their efforts to save Earth. In a last-ditch mind-meld using the Uni-Mind, Ikaris has a change of heart and helps Sersi turn the emerging Celestial, Tiamut, to stone instead — then flies guilt-ridden into the sun rather than face what he''d tried to do. Sersi turns Sprite fully human, three Eternals leave to warn others of what''s coming, and Sersi, Phastos and Kingo are abducted by the Celestial Arishem for judgment — while a mid-credits scene introduces Eros and Pip the Troll, and the post-credits scene has a mysterious voice asking whether Dane Whitman is ready to wield the cursed Ebony Blade.', duration = 156, director = 'Chloé Zhao', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 26;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/Spider-Man_No_Way_Home_poster.jpg', recap = 'With his identity now public and his loved ones'' lives falling apart, Peter Parker begs Doctor Strange to cast a memory-erasing spell, but Peter''s constant last-minute changes corrupt it and rip open the multiverse, pulling in villains from other Spider-Man realities — Green Goblin, Doc Ock, Electro, Sandman, and Lizard. Peter chooses to cure them instead of sending them home to their deaths, but the Goblin''s darker persona resurfaces and kills Aunt May, devastating Peter right as two alternate-universe Peter Parkers arrive to help him fight and heal the villains together. At the Statue of Liberty, the three Spider-Men defeat all five villains and cure most of them, and Peter asks Strange for one final spell: erase every memory of Peter Parker from existence, cutting himself off from MJ, Ned, and everyone he loves to protect the multiverse. He starts over completely alone, crafting a new homemade suit, while a mid-credits scene has Eddie Brock''s Venom symbiote merge briefly with this universe before splitting off and leaving a residue behind as Brock is pulled back to his own world.', duration = 148, director = 'Jon Watts', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 27;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/17/Doctor_Strange_in_the_Multiverse_of_Madness_poster.jpg', recap = 'A multiverse-jumping demon hunts teenager America Chavez, whose untrained powers can punch holes between realities, and Doctor Strange discovers the real threat is Wanda Maximoff, who has become the dark Scarlet Witch and wants to steal Chavez''s power to reunite with the children she conjured in WandaVision. Strange and Chavez flee to Earth-838, where they meet the Illuminati — Professor X, Captain Carter, Black Bolt, Captain Marvel, and Reed Richards — who are all brutally slaughtered by Wanda when she catches up and possesses her alternate self''s body. Strange briefly possesses his own corrupted-but-dead variant''s corpse using that universe''s evil Darkhold to fight back, and Chavez finally masters her powers to send Wanda home, where her own children recoil from her in horror. Wanda, confronted with what she''s become, destroys Mount Wundagore and every copy of the Darkhold across the multiverse, seemingly sacrificing herself — while a mid-credits scene has a mysterious sorceress warn Strange that his use of the Darkhold has torn open a dangerous "incursion" he now has to fix.', duration = 126, director = 'Sam Raimi', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 28;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/88/Thor_Love_and_Thunder_poster.jpeg', recap = 'Grief-maddened Gorr the God Butcher, after his daughter dies and his god ignores his prayers, claims the Necrosword and swears to wipe out every god in existence, eventually kidnapping New Asgard''s children as bait. Thor discovers his ex Jane Foster is dying of cancer and has reforged his shattered hammer Mjolnir to become the Mighty Thor, and together with Valkyrie and Korg they chase Gorr across the cosmos, getting rebuffed and imprisoned by a cowardly Zeus along the way. In the Shadow Realm, Jane''s cancer finally catches up with her mid-battle and she dies in Thor''s arms after they seemingly defeat Gorr together, whose dying wish — moved by witnessing real love — is for the wish-granting Eternity to resurrect his daughter rather than destroy all gods. Thor adopts Gorr''s daughter Love and keeps fighting as a father-hero duo, while a mid-credits scene shows a recovering Zeus sending his son Hercules after Thor for revenge, and the post-credits scene reunites Jane with Heimdall in Valhalla.', duration = 119, director = 'Taika Waititi', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 29;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3b/Black_Panther_Wakanda_Forever_poster.jpg', recap = 'Following T''Challa''s off-screen death from illness, Wakanda is besieged by outside powers hunting for vibranium while Shuri races to recreate the heart-shaped herb that grants Black Panther powers, all while a hidden underwater civilization called Talokan, led by the mutant god-king Namor, emerges demanding Wakanda hand over the scientist responsible for a vibranium-detecting device. After Namor attacks the capital and Queen Ramonda drowns trying to save a young scientist, Shuri gains Black Panther powers herself and initially seeks bloody vengeance against Namor and his people. Guided by a vision of her mother, she instead spares Namor''s life and negotiates peace between the two vibranium nations rather than continuing the cycle of violence. Shuri plants new heart-shaped herbs to secure Wakanda''s future, and in the film''s single credits scene, Nakia introduces Shuri to T''Challa''s secret son Toussaint — revealing T''Challa had a hidden heir all along.', duration = 161, director = 'Ryan Coogler', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 30;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/30/Ant-Man_and_the_Wasp_Quantumania_poster.jpg', recap = 'A signal from Scott Lang''s teenage daughter Cassie accidentally sucks the whole family into the Quantum Realm, where Janet van Dyne reveals she has a dark secret history with its ruthless tyrant, the time-traveling conqueror Kang the Conqueror. Kang forces Scott to retrieve a power core Janet sabotaged years ago by threatening Cassie, and after Kang betrays them anyway, captures Janet, and destroys Hank Pym''s ship, the family rallies its Quantum Realm allies — including a rebellion led by Cassie and a reformed M.O.D.O.K. (Darren Cross) — to fight back. Hope shrinks down to help Scott overpower Kang, and together they shove him and a burst of unstable Pym Particles into his own power core, seemingly destroying him for good. The family escapes back to normal size, but a mid-credits scene reveals a vast Council of Kangs — countless variants across the multiverse — mourning their fallen "lesser" counterpart and plotting next steps, while the post-credits scene ties into Loki season 2''s Victor Timely variant.', duration = 124, director = 'Peyton Reed', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 31;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/74/Guardians_of_the_Galaxy_Vol._3_poster.jpg', recap = 'The genetically-engineered Adam Warlock critically wounds Rocket during an attack on Knowhere, and the team discovers a kill switch in his body means only his creator, the megalomaniacal High Evolutionary, can save him — sending them on a mission through his monstrous animal-hybrid experiments. Flashbacks reveal Rocket''s origin: the High Evolutionary vivisected him as a baby raccoon alongside friends Lylla, Teefs, and Floor on Counter-Earth, planning to harvest Rocket''s brain and incinerate the rest before Rocket''s rescue attempt failed and he watched them die. The present-day Guardians, aided by an amnesiac alternate-timeline Gamora, storm Orgocorp and Counter-Earth, retrieve the override code, and revive Rocket just as he has a peaceful near-death vision reuniting with his lost friends. In the final battle they defeat the High Evolutionary''s forces and free his genetically modified children rather than kill him, and Peter Quill retires to Earth to reunite with his grandfather, handing leadership of a new-look Guardians roster to Rocket.', duration = 150, director = 'James Gunn', post_credits_scenes = 2 WHERE id = 32;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7a/The_Marvels_poster.jpg', recap = 'Kree leader Dar-Benn steals a Quantum Band and starts ripping holes in space-time to siphon resources — sun, water, atmosphere — from other planets to restore her collapsing homeworld Hala, whose supreme leader Carol Danvers destroyed years earlier. A side effect of Dar-Benn''s rampant jump points causes Carol, Monica Rambeau, and young superfan Kamala Khan to swap places every time any of them use their powers simultaneously, forcing the trio to learn to fight in sync as "the Marvels." After Dar-Benn steals Kamala''s own Quantum Band and tries wielding both bands at once, the resulting overload destroys her; Kamala manages to seal the interdimensional rupture from the other side, stranding herself, while Carol restores Hala''s dying sun. Monica gets rescued and pulled into a parallel universe in the mid-credits scene, greeted by an alternate Maria Rambeau (Binary) and a mutant Hank McCoy, while Kamala recruits Kate Bishop back on Earth to start assembling a new young-heroes team.', duration = 105, director = 'Nia DaCosta', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 33;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4c/Deadpool_%26_Wolverine_poster.jpg', recap = 'Retired mercenary Wade Wilson gets recruited by the Time Variance Authority, who reveal his entire universe is dying because its anchor being, Wolverine, is dead — so Wade sets off across the multiverse to find a Logan variant worth saving. He drags a reluctant, disgraced Logan into the Void, a multiversal dumping ground ruled by Charles Xavier''s psychic twin sister Cassandra Nova, where they team up with a resistance of forgotten variants including Laura/X-23, Elektra, Blade, and Gambit. Cassandra plans to use a "Time Ripper" device to unravel every remaining timeline in the multiverse, and Wade and Logan destroy it together in a mutual, self-sacrificing act that — thanks to their shared healing factors — they both actually survive. Logan chooses to stay behind in Wade''s now-stabilized universe as Cassandra dies, and the single post-credits scene reveals the "real" story behind Johnny Storm''s shocking on-screen death earlier in the film.', duration = 128, director = 'Shawn Levy', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 34;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/Captain_America_Brave_New_World_poster.jpg', recap = 'New Captain America Sam Wilson and his partner Joaquin Torres get pulled into a conspiracy after newly elected President Thaddeus Ross invites them to a summit to sign a treaty over a rare new metal, adamantium, discovered on a "Celestial Island" left behind by Tiamut''s petrified body — but the event is disrupted when mysteriously mind-controlled assassins attack, framing an innocent soldier named Bradley. Sam traces the conspiracy to imprisoned scientist Samuel Sterns, who has been manipulating Ross with life-extension pills while secretly using subliminal mind control to provoke international war over the adamantium. When Sam exposes the plot publicly, an emotionally shattered Ross transforms into the monstrous Red Hulk, and Sam manages to talk him back down to human form by invoking his estranged daughter Betty. Bradley is exonerated, Torres officially joins the Avengers roster, and Ross resigns and goes to prison — while Sterns, still imprisoned, warns Sam in the post-credits scene of "a coming attack from other worlds."', duration = 118, director = 'Julius Onah', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 35;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/90/Thunderbolts%2A_poster.jpg', recap = 'CIA director Valentina de Fontaine sends four of her off-book operatives — Yelena Belova, John Walker, Ava Starr (Ghost), and Antonia Dreykov (Taskmaster) — into a trap intending for them to kill each other and bury evidence of her illegal Sentry super-soldier program, but they escape together instead, freeing an amnesiac man named Bob from cryo-stasis along the way. Bob turns out to be unstable and terrifyingly powerful; Valentina rebrands him publicly as the hero "Sentry" to save her political career, but a triggered failsafe unleashes his destructive alter-ego, the Void, who blankets New York in supernatural darkness that traps people in their worst memories. Yelena leads the team into the darkness to reach Bob''s traumatized psyche directly, and rather than fight him, they hug him and affirm their belief in him, letting him regain control and banish the Void. Valentina spins the team''s heroics into a press-conference win, publicly branding them the "New Avengers" and taking credit for assembling them, while a post-credits scene set 14 months later has the team detecting an extradimensional spacecraft marked with a giant "4" — the Fantastic Four''s ship arriving in their universe.', duration = 127, director = 'Jake Schreier', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 36;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/13/The_Fantastic_Four_First_Steps_poster.jpg', recap = 'Set on the retro-futuristic alternate Earth-828, the Fantastic Four celebrate four years as heroes just as Reed and Sue announce a pregnancy, right before the Silver Surfer arrives warning that the planet-devouring Galactus has marked Earth for destruction. The team confronts Galactus in space, who senses their unborn child carries immense cosmic potential and offers to spare Earth in exchange for the baby; they refuse and flee, with Sue giving birth to baby Franklin during the escape. Reed''s public reveal of the encounter sparks mass panic demanding Franklin''s sacrifice, so the team builds a mass-teleportation bridge to evacuate all of Earth''s population instead, while the Silver Surfer — revealed as the redeemed Shalla-Bal — tries to sabotage it under Galactus''s orders before Johnny talks her back to their side. Using baby Franklin as bait, the team lures Galactus to a final portal in Times Square; Sue uses her full power to force him through it while Shalla-Bal sacrifices herself sealing it, and the film ends on the team''s fifth anniversary — with a mid-credits scene, four years later, showing a mysterious cloaked man in a metal mask appearing in the Richards'' home with young Franklin.', duration = 114, director = 'Matt Shakman', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 37;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Spider-Man_Brand_New_Day_poster.jpg', recap = 'Four years after Doctor Strange''s spell erased the world''s memory of his identity, Peter Parker operates as an anonymous, full-time Spider-Man protecting New York. When a powerful telepathic mutant, Jean Grey, begins attacking the Department of Damage Control while hunting for her missing sister Sara, Peter''s own powers start evolving unpredictably. Teaming up with Frank Castle and Bruce Banner, Peter uncovers that the DODC was responsible for Sara''s death, and helps a grieving Jean find peace rather than fighting her as an enemy. A post-credits scene shows Ned''s "Spidey Tracker" app pinging Spider-Man''s location as somewhere out in deep space.', duration = 145, director = 'Destin Daniel Cretton', post_credits_scenes = 1 WHERE id = 38;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ee/Avengers_Doomsday_poster.jpg', recap = 'Roughly 14 months after Thunderbolts*, heroes from across the multiverse — the Avengers, the New Avengers, the Fantastic Four, Wakanda, and the X-Men — converge against Doctor Doom. Full plot details are not yet public; this recap will be corrected once the film has released.', duration = 165, director = 'Anthony Russo, Joe Russo', post_credits_scenes = 0 WHERE id = 39;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE films SET poster_url = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Marvel_Studios_2016_logo.svg', recap = 'The fourth and final chapter of the Multiverse Saga. Plot details, cast, and a poster have not yet been released; this recap will be corrected once the film has released.', duration = 150, director = 'Anthony Russo, Joe Russo', post_credits_scenes = 0 WHERE id = 40;
